c890f76d983266" :answer-field/choices ["q-43836/selection/d1df95784514e1c50aeadd708d8ada50a5cf04e1a8cba1c5c3c890f76d983266" "q-43836/selection/3ad18ee62d82c8c2b30efcb5dc424d011d8da146e4791fdecacb962b6f319810" "q-43836/selection/913a80b7cfeba5ad57aed8c6cf7a82ff7165b7ee9f2325f34db276caee6df10e" "q-43836/selection/daf6e933578b9d5e340809e309cafbb767a31f415f7f3df6f309328a663f4fc2" "q-43836/selection/c9927a29f704c907382d4104030554305368308698b30ec24a2f2e8e422216fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43836" :question/id #uuid "893af612-df42-5399-b5a5-36237571f3e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-43836" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i,j}$ of ${R}^{2}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i$ and $T\\cdot j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-43836/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556"] :knowledge-point/